# A transformed permanent has only its back face's characteristics, but its mana value is calculated from its front face's
# mana cost (CR 202.3b, 712.8e; Ashling's ruling: "the mana value of a nonmodal double-faced card is the mana value of its
# front face, no matter which face is up"). Ashling, Rimebound has no mana cost and mana value 2 ({1}{R}). Bot2's
# Prismatic Ending with X of 1, paid with two Plains, had one color of mana spent on it, so it exiles nothing of mana value
# 2. The second, with X of 2 paid with white, black and green mana, had three, and exiles Ashling.

